        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Title page, author affiliations, and abstract for \"Indexing by Latent Semantic Analysis\" by Scott Deerwester (University of Chicago), Susan T. Dumais, George W. Furnas, and Thomas K. Landauer (Bellcore), and Richard Harshman (University of Western Ontario), published in JASIS 41(6), 391–407 (1990). The abstract introduces automatic indexing and retrieval via singular value decomposition (SVD), decomposing a large term-by-document matrix into roughly 100 orthogonal factors so that documents are represented as factor-weight vectors, queries are formed as pseudo-document vectors from weighted term combinations, and documents exceeding a cosine similarity threshold are retrieved.",
