        "text": "Concluding Section 3.1 and beginning Section 3.2 (The choice of method for uncovering latent semantic structure). Higher-order correlational structure can also down-weight polysemous \"imposter\" terms like \"information\" in Doc 2 when surrounding context does not support the intended meaning. Section 3.2 surveys proximity models (hierarchical, partition, and overlapping clustering, ultrametric/additive trees, latent class analysis, and factor analysis) and critiques hierarchical document or term clustering as too restrictive because hierarchies forbid cross-classifications, have only O(n) free parameters for n objects, and improve search efficiency without clear evidence of improving retrieval effectiveness.",
